  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Operationalization of Mobile Primary Healthcare Units in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of the response to the ongoing crisis in Sudan, this project seeks to enhance the health, nutrition and mental well-being of internally displaced persons and other migrants as well as host communities by improving the accessibility and availability of primary healthcare services, including mental health support and health promotion. The interventions aim to directly address the heightened risks of infectious diseases, malnutrition resulting from food and water insecurity, trauma-related psychiatric disorders, and other vulnerabilities. The focus on infectious diseases encompasses Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV), tuberculosis (TB) and malaria, with close coordination involving the National HIV and TB Programmes, Federal and State Ministry of Health and UNDP.</narrative>
  </description>
